ownbeat and almost like  an la version of mumble core micro  budget movies about creatives aimlessly  searching for themselves  you hate women  what  as if all of donald glover's  accomplishments weren't enough he also  made emmy's history when he received two  accolades for his work on atlanta  outstanding directing for a comedy  series as well as outstanding lead actor  in a comedy series glover became the  first black director to win in the  comedy category understandably it was  all a bit overwhelming i  i blacked out i don't know yeah like i  was not ready for that  he explained further saying he was in a  weird phase when he directed ban the  episode for which he won his emmy i was  doing a lot okay i was like a new father  okay writing other episodes and  directing and like cobbling this  together  he went on to say i'm really astonished  i was really shocked  one of the most bizarre and disturbing  episodes of atlanta was season two's  teddy perkins in this episode earn an  alfred's stoner philosopher friend  darius shows up to a large house outside  the city to pick up a free piano  there he encounters teddy perkins a  reclusive light-skinned face-lifted  former songwriter who is also played by  glover teddy insists on giving darius a  tour of the house which doubles as a  museum dedicated to himself and his  brother who lives in the attic suffice  to say things get very creepy very  quickly this is the furthest atlanta has  tipped into outright horror at least in  its first three seasons it was made all  the more unsettling when glover brought  his terrifying creation into the real  world apparently dressing is teddy  perkins at the 2018 emmy awards when he  was nominated for best actor in a comedy  series the word apparently is important  here because later in the evening glover  and teddy perkins were somehow  photographed together so who was sitting  in glover's seat internet sleuths  scoured the possibilities for months an  e-news report at the time quoted a  source claiming that the person under  the makeup was former snl cast member  jay pharaoh which pharaoh all but  confirmed in a 2021 video interview with  conde nast traveler had to be somebody  under there right  had to be somebody  three hours of makeup  in 2018 childish gambino released this  is america the song and its accompanying  hero mirai directed video was an  immediate viral hit it launched a  thousand think pieces scouring its every  lyric and image for meaning mirai  presents the bulk of the video as a  single take following glover through an  empty warehouse alternating between  moments of joy to moments of shocking  violence  likewise the music crashes buoyant  caribbean inspired rhythms up against  the haunting drone of its chorus glover  performed the song when he hosted  saturday night live that year and a  version of it also appeared in glover's  2019 short film guava island it also  became the first rap song to ever win  song of the year at the grammys glover's  work elicited a number of negative  reactions as well with some taking issue  with what they saw as his exploiting  black trauma and violence under the  guise of making art he's also been  accused of plagiarism on more than one  occasion in 2018 fans noted the  similarities between this is america and  rapper jace harley's 2016 song american  pharaoh harley declined to take legal  action apparently grateful just to be  part of the conversation in 2021 however  the rapper kid wes filed a suit against  glover on behalf of his own 2016 song  made in america glover maintains that  this is america predates both harley and  kid west's tracks  season 3 of atlanta premiered in march  2022 after a four-year hiatus during  that time one of glover's most high  profile gigs was the 2019 live action  remake of disney's the lion king  director john favreau and an army of  visual effects artists crafted a new  version of the classic 1994 animated  film and photorealistic cgi but  crucially retained the original film's  award-winning songs this meant that  glover playing simba had to sing the  well-known duet can you feel the love  tonight with nala played in the remake  by beyonce knowles carter glover was in  london filming solo a star wars story at  the time so he recorded his vocals  separately which as he joked on jimmy  kimmel live was probably a good thing  for him i did not want to be looking  into beyonce's eyes while doing  this  despite being an acclaimed recording  artist in his own right having to match  pipes with beyonce in the same room  would be a pretty nerve-wracking thing  in the segment kimmel suggests that it  was probably less intimidating to record  separately glover agrees i imagine it's  less intimidating playing basketball  with michael jordan yeah if you're at  home just throwing  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite celebrities are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one
 

